--TEST--
a `foreach` binding is a use site like any other, so iterating an `array<tainted string>` colours the binding — and the local it goes on to name — `tainted`, while the array holding them carries nothing itself, `rule:security/tainted-qualifier`, `rule:ide/semantic-tokens-carry-the-qualifiers`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Handler {
    public function handle(array<tainted string> $chunks): void {
        foreach ($chunks as tainted string $chunk) {
            var $seen = $chunk;
        }
    }
}
--REQUEST--
semanticTokens
--EXPECT--
2:7+7 class
3:21+6 method
3:50+7 parameter
4:18+7 variable
4:44+6 variable tainted
5:17+5 variable tainted
5:25+6 variable tainted
